      "title": "INFO — Models & optimization",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Model setup\n- **H3 FL2VA Diffusion Model:** supports the flexible T2VA / I2VA / L2VA / FL2VA conditioning used here.\n- **Qwen3-VL H3 Encoder:** encodes the prompt plus all connected Picture inputs.\n- **Video / Audio VAE:** decode H3's two latent streams.\n- **SageAttention:** optional speed/memory optimization used by this example.\n\nKeep the same model/VAE setup for every clip in one chain.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1550,
        990
      ],
      "size": [
        1120,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 24,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Optional keyframes & Qwen References",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Image inputs and Picture mapping\n**First Frame** and **Last Frame are optional.** Connect neither, either one, or both depending on whether you want T2VA, I2VA, L2VA or FL2VA behavior.\n\nWhen both keyframes and Qwen References are connected, Picture numbering is deterministic:\n- `Picture 1 = First Frame`\n- `Picture 2 = Last Frame`\n- `Picture 3 = Qwen Reference 1`\n- additional Qwen References continue as Picture 4, 5, ...\n\nIf a keyframe is omitted, numbering closes the gap automatically. The node's `picture_map` output and console log show the exact mapping used for the run.\n\n**Qwen Reference 1** is Qwen-only guidance, not a native Ref2VA/DiT reference latent. Connecting it automatically reveals **Qwen Reference 2**, then 3, and so on up to nine.\n\nFor long-form continuation, First/Last keyframes are optional technically but **recommended as quality-reset anchors**, particularly the Last Frame.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 27,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -300,
        910
      ],
      "size": [
        630,
        350
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 25,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Flexible Start / Conditioning v1.4",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### H3 Infinite - Flexible Start / Conditioning v1.4\nThe Start node intentionally keeps the proven v1.3 Picture/conditioning behavior.\n\n- **Prompt:** action, dialogue, camera motion and audio intent.\n- **Width / Height:** keep constant across the chain.\n- **Duration:** requested seconds; H3 snaps to its valid temporal grid.\n- **ref_image_size:** `match` is the recommended normal setting.\n\nConnected First/Last Frames are native temporal keyframes and also receive the first Qwen Picture numbers. Extra Qwen References follow afterward. Use the node's `picture_map` output as the authoritative mapping.\n\nExample with First + Last + one reference: `Picture 1 = First`, `Picture 2 = Last`, `Picture 3 = Qwen Reference 1`."
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 28,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        390,
        830
      ],
      "size": [
        770,
        310
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 26,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Sampling settings",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Sampling\nThe example uses **Sigma Shift 12 / 3**, `res_multistep`, **15 steps**, and a random seed.\n\nThese are normal H3 sampling controls, not continuation-specific. Change them if your H3 setup requires different values. For consistent behavior, use the same sampling setup for all clips in the chain.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 29,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1580,
        1020
      ],
      "size": [
        640,
        350
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 27,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Auto Handover",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Auto Handover — v1.4 v1.4\nAuto Handover determines the **actual visual continuation boundary** for Native Masked AV.\n\nIt first finds a safe point before the FL2VA freeze / unstable Last-Frame landing, then snaps backward to the latest exact Masked-AV video boundary.\n\nThat boundary is used twice:\n- `Stitch Ready` keeps this clip only through that safe video frame.\n- The next `Continue — Native Masked AV` protects the safe video context ending at the same frame.\n\nv1.4 keeps this proven validated video geometry unchanged. Audio can now remain protected farther than the visual cut when valid original dialogue continues into the discarded video tail. `Balanced` remains the recommended detector preset."
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1230,
        790
      ],
      "size": [
        350,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 28,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Save AV Latent",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Save the full AV latent\nThe Save node always stores the **complete, untrimmed** video + audio latent and the Auto Handover metadata. Clip 1 has no reused head, so its saved `head_context_frames` is 0.\n\nKeep the numbered files if you plan to continue later **or combine separately generated clips with the `04 — Stitch Saved Chain` workflow**.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#3f3f3f",
      "bgcolor": "#575757"
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        2030,
        560
      ],
      "size": [
        820,
        340
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 29,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "INFO — Full / Stitch Ready / Final Clip",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Output / Stitch\n**Full:** complete decoded clip.  \n**Stitch Ready:** intermediate clip; ends at the exact freeze/brightness-safe Masked-AV video boundary selected by Auto Handover.  \n**Final Clip:** keeps the complete ending of the current final segment. If you also want freeze safety at the very end, use `Stitch Ready` for the final segment.\n\nThe exact Masked-AV grid can move the safe video boundary several good frames earlier than the detector's ideal pixel cut. v1.4 deliberately accepts this conservative loss because later-frame recovery produced visible motion/alignment errors in live testing. **Safe Tail Bridge therefore defaults to 0** and remains Advanced for legacy/A-B use. Luminance matching is also an Advanced fallback and stays OFF."
      ],
      "color": "#66511f",
      "bgcolor": "#8a6d28"
    }
